WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.645
When the weather turned warm, the earl and his wife left Earlshall Park.

2
00:00:07.646 --> 00:00:11.398
They wanted to spend time in London with some family members.

3
00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:15.352
Most of the horses were left behind, including Ginger and me.

4
00:00:15.353 --> 00:00:21.841
Mr. York went with the earl, leaving a senior groom named Reuben Smith in charge of the stable.

5
00:00:21.842 --> 00:00:31.370
The earl's two oldest daughters, Lady Harriet and Lady Anne, stayed at home with one of their brothers and some cousins who had come to visit for the summer.

6
00:00:31.371 --> 00:00:38.053
Lady Harriet was a sickly young woman who never went out in the carriage and rarely showed her face outdoors.

7
00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:43.224
Her sister, Lady Anne, on the other hand, was as lively and healthy as could be.

8
00:00:43.225 --> 00:00:50.356
She loved to spend time outside, and she went riding as often as she could with her brothers and cousins.

9
00:00:50.357 --> 00:00:55.232
Soon she became my primary rider, renaming me Black Auster.

10
00:00:55.233 --> 00:01:01.085
I enjoyed our rides very much. Lady Anne was an excellent horsewoman.

11
00:01:01.086 --> 00:01:05.303
Her hands were light, and her mood was always cheerful.

12
00:01:05.304 --> 00:01:09.852
Her favorite riding companion was a cousin named Blantyre.

13
00:01:09.853 --> 00:01:16.664
While some of the young men liked to ride Ginger, Blantyre's favorite was a different mare known as Lizzie.

14
00:01:16.665 --> 00:01:22.318
Lizzie was a bright bay with a smooth, fast canter and a lively spirit.

15
00:01:22.319 --> 00:01:29.398
Young Blantyre was always telling anyone who would listen what a fine horse she was.

16
00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:36.144
But Ginger, who knew Lizzie better than I did, once told me that Lizzie was rather nervous.

17
00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:43.036
One day when Lady Anne came to the stable, she asked the groom to put the sidesaddle on Lizzie.

18
00:01:43.037 --> 00:01:47.162
The sidesaddle was the type of saddle always used by young women.

19
00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:52.208
Lady Anne also said that Blantyre could ride me that day.

20
00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:57.828
When the young man himself arrived, he seemed surprised and a bit uneasy.

21
00:01:57.829 --> 00:02:03.041
"What's going on?" he asked Lady Anne. "Are you tired of Black Auster?"

22
00:02:03.042 --> 00:02:06.911
"Of course not!" she replied with a laugh.

23
00:02:06.912 --> 00:02:10.739
"But I'm nice enough to let you ride him just this once.

24
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:16.375
And after all the good things you've said about Lizzie, I can't wait to try her myself!"

25
00:02:16.376 --> 00:02:20.600
"I'm not sure that's a good idea," Blantyre said.

26
00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:25.415
"Lizzie is a charming creature, but she's much too nervous for a lady.

27
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:27.867
I don't think it's safe for you to ride her.

28
00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:31.518
Please, let's have the saddles switched back."

29
00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:34.952
Lady Anne just laughed.

30
00:02:34.953 --> 00:02:40.619
"My dear cousin, you don't have to worry about my safety!" she exclaimed.

31
00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.483
"I've been riding since I was a baby.

32
00:02:43.484 --> 00:02:47.008
Now stop looking so worried and help me mount."

33
00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:50.389
Blantyre bit his lip, but said no more.

34
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:57.297
He helped her into the saddle, handed her the reins, and then mounted me.

35
00:02:57.298 --> 00:03:01.962
We were riding toward the gate when we heard someone calling.

36
00:03:01.963 --> 00:03:04.458
It was one of the house servants.

37
00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:11.313
"Lady Harriet has a question for Dr. Ashley," he said, holding up a slip of paper.

38
00:03:11.314 --> 00:03:15.851
"Would you mind delivering this note to his house and bringing back an answer?"

39
00:03:15.852 --> 00:03:21.407
"Certainly," Blantyre said, taking the note. "We'd be happy to help."

40
00:03:21.408 --> 00:03:25.498
The village where the doctor lived was about a mile away.

41
00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:28.272
We rode along at a pleasant walk.

42
00:03:28.273 --> 00:03:33.547
Blantyre was a good rider, and I was enjoying the exercise in the fresh air.

43
00:03:33.548 --> 00:03:36.446
Lizzie seemed to be having a good time as well.

44
00:03:36.447 --> 00:03:41.333
She was giving Lady Anne no trouble at all.

45
00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:44.226
We pulled up in front of the doctor's gate.

46
00:03:44.227 --> 00:03:49.492
There was a short path leading between some tall evergreens that hid the house from view.

47
00:03:49.493 --> 00:03:53.275
"Go ahead and take the note in," Lady Anne told her cousin.

48
00:03:53.276 --> 00:03:55.912
"Lizzie and I will wait for you here.

49
00:03:55.913 --> 00:04:01.368
You can hang Black Auster's rein on the gate— he won't go anywhere without you."

50
00:04:01.369 --> 00:04:05.898
Blantyre looked dubious. "Are you sure you'll be all right?"

51
00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:12.699
"Of course. Now go!" she said with a laugh.

52
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:15.795
Blantyre dismounted and hung my reins on the fence.

53
00:04:15.796 --> 00:04:18.462
Then he disappeared between the trees.

54
00:04:18.463 --> 00:04:23.065
Lizzie was standing quietly by the side of the road on a loose rein.

55
00:04:23.066 --> 00:04:26.620
Lady Anne was smiling and humming a cheerful tune.

56
00:04:26.621 --> 00:04:30.828
We were right across the road from an open gate leading into a field.

57
00:04:30.829 --> 00:04:38.154
While we were waiting for Blantyre to return, some horses suddenly came trotting across the field, jumping and kicking.

58
00:04:38.155 --> 00:04:42.812
A boy was chasing them, cracking a large whip.

59
00:04:42.813 --> 00:04:48.256
Before I knew what was happening, one of the horses spotted the open gate and darted through it.

60
00:04:48.257 --> 00:04:54.173
The boy saw the escape and raced over, yelling and cracking the whip loudly.

61
00:04:54.174 --> 00:04:57.967
The colt raced across the road, bumping into Lizzie's hind end.

62
00:04:57.968 --> 00:05:00.876
Just then the whip let out another loud crack.

63
00:05:00.877 --> 00:05:06.950
"Oh!" Lady Anne cried, barely hanging on to the saddle as her horse gave a violent kick.

64
00:05:06.951 --> 00:05:13.598
A second later Lizzie bolted down the road at a headlong gallop.

